WEBVTT

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.600
It's wrong. It's all wrong...

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:45.510
Stop.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:48.340
Stop it!

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:55.260
Over there...

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.090
That's the real world.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:02.760
Stay away, Kaminagi!

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:06.160
STAY AWAY!

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:21.480
Kaminagi!

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.390
It's morning already.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:47.140
Morning is coming...

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:57.120
Did Kaminagi...
Did Kaminagi come here?!

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:00.690
Kaminagi who?

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.730
Ryoko Kaminagi!

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.990
Oh. Your girlfriend?

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:11.260
I saw a cereb-icon appear on her!
So, did she come here?!

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:16.330
There are several other potential
awakeners on the Maihama server.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.980
Right now, the Oceanus crew are
very busy analyzing their data.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.030
I'm reading the activation of another Cerebrant mode!

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.190
Maihama Minami high school, in front of the main gate.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.190
The Tomigai shop, right?

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.400
Tomigai?!

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.910
We've got a bumper crop this time, huh?

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.910
Are we prepared for them?

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:52.400
They're being brought into our contact network
under the guise of the student council.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:56.010
Our contact network, huh?

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.350
Aside from that, have you managed
to trace where the Kobral landed?

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:02.490
We're still analyzing the data, so...

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:04.620
A Cerebrant hunt will take some time.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:07.530
Minato, continue the analysis.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.260
Aye, sir!

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.460
A Cerebrant hunt, huh?

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:14.870
We called it the harvest festival
back in the Shanghai server.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:17.570
But hunting is what they call it here.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.800
What are you up to?!
Hey, you!

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:22.130
Kyo!

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:25.400
Want some tea?

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:41.360
What gives? Why me? Why do I have
to take supplementary lessons?

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:47.290
They called you in, too?

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.370
Yeah, the dreaded e-mail arrived.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:52.390
I didn't think I did <i>that bad</i> at the end of the term!

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:58.970
Hayase... They're teaching the second
and third year students together?

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.950
Isn't Kaminagi coming to this, too?

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:09.080
She already has an excellent alternative
to supplementary lessons, doesn't she?

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.260
Nothing.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:17.830
So, what are these "supplementary lessons," anyway?

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.090
Something wrong?

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.200
Is there something on my face?

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:33.710
It's cute!

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:42.550
What's this?

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.020
Is the class starting?

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:46.860
What's with the numbers?

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:47.550
Is this math class?

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.620
What the?!

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:55.770
What are you showing them?

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:56.940
Well?

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:59.200
Still no reaction.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:14.280
Sogoru...

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.290
It's Kyo!

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:17.590
Me?

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:22.230
We're presenting your meta-body data during
combat as a mathematical progression.

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:24.990
And you're saying they can tell
what it is?! Those two can?!

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.670
They can tell that it's <i>you.</i>

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:32.270
But it looks like they can't
read that it's combat data.

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:35.570
Are those two Cerebrants?!

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:37.640
Just them?

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:41.170
Yes. That's it.
What do we do with them?

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.980
I'm not after bridge personnel right now.
Save them for later.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:48.050
Hey! Mr. President!

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:50.260
Are you sure about this?!

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:52.690
The meta-bodies within
the Maihama server...

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:55.960
Do you find it a contradiction?

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:59.730
That we make those we have
to protect join the battle?

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:01.700
A big one!

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:03.100
I suppose.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:08.530
Still, it's very rare to have so
many candidates appear at once.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:11.600
We have pretty high hopes
for this batch.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:16.780
Although, we only have a couple of
strong candidates at the moment.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:23.860
What's up? Why'd they ask just us two to stay behind?

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:26.430
Not a clue.

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:30.620
But not many people mature to be true Cerebrants.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:35.700
If they don't grow into them before the
server resets, we have to start over.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:40.640
Resets? What are you talking about?

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:46.280
But I get you. Awakening doesn't
automatically make you a Cerebrant!

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:48.550
Odds are, they aren't ripe yet!

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:52.710
Exactly, meaning it's not certain
that your girlfriend is one yet.

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:01.890
No, that's nothing to smile about.

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:05.760
Commander. We have the analysis results.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:16.280
The Kobral headed north.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:20.080
We can't get an exact fix on
where its flight path terminated,

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.510
but it was definitely along this course.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:27.080
Arque left us one last gift.

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:35.830
All right. Tell Chris about this, too.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:37.930
I'll do it!

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:43.090
It's not healthy to avoid sleep like this.

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:47.800
I'm fine.
I get enough rest just from this.

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:49.400
But...

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:54.810
In the stress of combat,
you're terrified to even blink.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:57.870
Just doing this is heaven to me.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:08:59.620
Even with me here?

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:05.550
You calm me down. Your silly
chatter is just what I need right now.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.780
I hoped you'd say that.

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:11.990
Chris! We found it! The Gards-orm stronghold!

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:14.930
Where?!

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:27.240
<i>Even I could understand this.</i>

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.750
<i>The burning need</i>
<i>Chris felt to train harder.</i>

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:38.260
<i>The need he felt to avenge Arque.</i>

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:44.390
<i>A need that could only be satisfied</i>
<i>by striking the enemy's main base.</i>

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:54.240
I appreciate your
taking care of Pieta.

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:58.670
He's a cute puppy. It's fun, the way he races around.

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:00.610
Just do as good a job back there, too.

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:03.520
Right. Deploying holonic rifle!

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:07.750
Oh, but first, I'll turn away from
the target drones' flight path.

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:10.310
Just take it slow.

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:12.590
You just want it done instantly.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:18.000
It's the urge to pair up quickly
to get back in the fight.

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:23.570
Whoa, there!

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:25.440
I'm sorry!

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:26.810
Nah, it was fun!

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:30.210
Dare 'em to hit us!
We'll let 'em destroy each other!

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:32.700
And detonate the
missiles trailing us, too!

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:39.920
Everyone has high hopes
for this training, too.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:42.010
They must be hoping to
find even one new pilot.

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:44.980
That's right.

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:50.860
You only really want pilots from this crop
of awakening Cerebrants, don't you?

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:55.630
But can't you make an exception?
Just for Kaminagi?

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:57.040
Why?

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:59.710
Not her. Anyone but her.

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:01.270
Why?

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:03.500
Because I've sworn to protect her.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.010
She's what you fight to protect?

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:08.480
Yeah.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:09.340
Fine.

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:14.410
But you're not the one
who decides this.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:16.180
What do you mean?

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:32.530
Happy Sogoru. Angry Sogoru.

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:36.840
Kyo today, Kyo yesterday.
Kyo, Kyo, Kyo...

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:40.610
A whole lotta Kyo, huh?
Is this file the same?

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:44.780
<i>I'm not lying! Kaminagi,</i>
<i>I really do!</i>

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:46.720
Agh! That's enough!

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:53.130
So, did you learn anything?

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:58.090
Yeah, that I've had a bellyful of your
desire to take pictures of Kyo!

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:01.800
But something's still missing...

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:04.200
Is that the question
a film director would ask?

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:11.040
They'd wonder if they'd captured
what it is that <i>he's</i> seeing.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:13.780
You're right.

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:17.370
My dear Ryoko, how about
taking some shots of yourself?

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:22.750
No, I'm not what Kyo's looking at.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:24.750
What?

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:31.760
Honestly, I've only just lately
started to figure out what it is.

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:36.800
But just as I can put it
into words, it drifts away.

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:45.280
Sis! Play Wizard for me!
Being a Gunner by myself is too hard!

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:53.310
These Gornes are so slippery,
and their defenses are hard!

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:57.150
See? It just closed up again.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.750
Just calm down
and you'll be fine.

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:09.000
Incoming!

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.770
Deploying launcher.
Aim for the ocean!

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.160
The ocean?

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:22.210
See? They open the armor when they fire.

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:25.080
I see.
So, that's what you aim at.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:33.750
Right. We can't give up
defending this world.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:43.860
<i>Someone has been</i>
<i>protecting us for a long time.</i>

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:52.970
Is training over?

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:01.020
Kaminagi.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:03.690
Oh. What's up?

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:06.490
Kyo...

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:11.990
Look... I'm not sure
how to put this, but...

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:18.660
I've become a Cerebrant, like you.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:24.540
Wha... What do you mean,
a Cerebrant?

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.280
I know.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:33.890
It's hot, huh?
Naturally, since it's summer.

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:35.750
Wanna go get some ice cream?

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:45.830
Here. It's all ready.
That'll be 400 yen, please.

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:51.740
Just kidding. It's free!

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:55.370
Who'll get angry
if we eat it, anyway?

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.650
Kaminagi!

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:09.010
I know. This world's artificial.

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:13.180
A movie set.
Like a big backdrop, right?

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:19.800
So, how long have you been
keeping it to yourself, Kyo?

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:24.000
Don't say any more. I mean...
It's better if you didn't know.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:24.900
Why?

00:15:28.270 --> 00:15:30.570
Let's have some fun!
Why waste the chance?

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:32.240
Have fun?

00:15:40.820 --> 00:15:42.790
No way...

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.420
Wanna go for a drive?

00:15:46.390 --> 00:15:48.260
You've got a license, right?

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:52.530
Now look... I have one,
but not for a two-seater!

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:57.260
Well, that's not like you.
Worrying about that stuff in a virtual world!

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.200
Should I drive, then?

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:05.740
Although...
I think the back seat suits me more.

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:10.210
Why fight it?

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:14.980
Don't blame me
for whatever happens!

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:18.190
I'll be fine!

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:27.990
Got it!

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:32.430
Ryoko Kaminagi
has matured as a pilot.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:37.540
Well, there it is.

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:42.010
She seems to have matured to
accept the change in her situation...

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:44.240
more flexibly than anyone else.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:49.610
I was like that too when I was
salvaged from the Sydney server.

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:55.630
So, what's up?
Why isn't anyone coming?

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:56.920
Like I know?

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:00.900
How far do we go?

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:02.590
Forever!

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.770
What, is that impossible?

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:07.930
Uh, yeah.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:12.340
Then... I wanna see
the edge of this world!

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:14.010
The edge?

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:17.620
Don't wanna?

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:20.110
I didn't say no. It's just...

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:21.420
What?

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:22.750
Not sayin'!

00:17:25.260 --> 00:17:27.990
Feels nice going this fast, doesn't it?

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:28.960
Yeah.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:32.030
Like you've one with the wind?

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:33.430
Puh-lease!

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:36.400
See, that's why I didn't
want to say it before!

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:43.570
Take a left there!

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:46.580
Now a right!

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.510
Huh?

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:50.150
Am I being a pain?

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:53.050
No. It's just...

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:00.360
That settles it.

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:04.060
You and I entering
this world changed it.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:10.160
It's all right, isn't it?
Considering the outcome.

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:13.030
It's beginning, isn't it?
With those two.

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:21.850
Angry that she's taken
the rear seat, are you?

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:37.630
Come on.

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:41.590
Stay with me.

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:50.270
This is the edge, huh?
We can't go any further, can we?

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:52.340
Right.

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:57.980
We can't leave Maihama, can we? So...

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:00.880
Sorry, but we can't go
to Shibuya, either.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:03.720
Even in the other world?

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:06.460
Even in the real world?

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:08.520
Tokyo is...

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:13.400
Just like in the game, huh?
That's awful...

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:14.590
Still...

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:18.200
We can cross the sea
on the other side.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:19.040
Oh?

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.570
And the ocean
is so beautiful there!

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:22.730
Wow...

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:25.810
No fair.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.510
No fair?

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.040
I want to see it with you.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.610
Show me, Kyo.

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:36.280
The real world.

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:43.030
Listen, the people in this
world are all alive, though.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:45.160
Hold it there!

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:51.290
Hey!

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:55.430
I want to take pictures
of the real world.

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:59.810
I've decided the film we'll
shoot this summer will be...

00:19:59.810 --> 00:20:02.650
a documentary from
your point of view, Kyo!

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:04.050
Mine?

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:08.640
Everything in this world
is all fiction, right?

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:10.960
I guess so.

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:13.430
Realistic orange, huh?

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:15.550
Nice and warm.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:20.420
And I know.
That everyone in this world is alive.

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:25.940
Mizuki and Koji and Tomigai...

00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:29.130
You, Kyo... Everyone is alive.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:31.310
But, there were times...

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:35.210
Times I realized there was
something wrong with this world.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:38.580
And it was so sad.
So hard to take.

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:40.690
Same with me.

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:44.180
I felt alone. So helpless.

00:20:46.690 --> 00:20:49.460
You don't want to
take me there with you?

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:52.160
I didn't say that. It's just...

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:53.030
Just what?

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:55.360
Oh, I'm not saying it this time!

00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:02.070
What's that?

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:04.740
That's your answer.

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:10.250
Should we go back?

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:11.510
Sure.

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:54.290
To be a Gunner or
Wizard is a sort of talent.

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:56.920
And Ryoko Kaminagi
has that sort of talent!

00:22:56.920 --> 00:22:59.790
I can hardly believe it myself!

00:22:59.790 --> 00:23:01.760
She said you and I make a good couple.

00:23:01.760 --> 00:23:03.330
What a wonderful girl!

00:23:03.330 --> 00:23:06.430
However, it looks like she's
going to cause all sorts of strife.

00:23:06.430 --> 00:23:08.600
She will? I suppose so...

00:23:08.600 --> 00:23:12.330
She will! By the tastiness
of this rice ball, she will!

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:16.240
Next time, on Zegapain:
"A New Wizard."

00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:18.880
My thoughts, never to be erased.
